DATABASE SETUP:

Activities store start_at and end_at as UTC DATETIME values, with date retaining
the club-local session-start business day. db/SqlConnector.js sets each borrowed
connection's session time zone to '+00:00'; it does not rely on the host's TZ
or the MySQL server's default time zone.

MySQL named time zone tables must be loaded for CONVERT_TZ to resolve 'UTC'
and each club's IANA time zone, on every platform. Migration 0016 checks this
before backfilling activity instants. Setting the host's TZ alone does not
populate those tables. See database_schema/migrations/README.md for upgrades.

Connect to Database Running in a container
docker exec -it name_of_container bash

Env Variables
server.js loads .env through dotenv. Container deployments can supply environment
variables through their deployment configuration. db/SqlConnector.js reads
SQL_HOST, SQL_PORT, SQL_USER, SQL_PASSWORD, and SQL_DATABASE; CLUB_ID scopes the
backend to one club.

Credential files
Firebase handles user authentication. firebaseadmin/firebaseadmin.js uses
applicationDefault() to obtain runtime credentials; it does not read a fixed
/cred/ path. Configure application default credentials for the deployment.
